    "reason": "With sein and no reflexive the verb is directional motion back to a place ('in ihre Heimatstadt zurückgezogen'). 'Retreat' is reflexive sich zurückziehen (haben), already carried by the sibling 'withdraw, pull back'. 'move away' names the opposite direction from zurück, which is worse than imprecise. Per-lemma candidates cover only the haben senses, which the dual-auxiliary caveat says is not grounds to reject."
  },
  "überkochen#0": {
